rkzc: what is in this package, under which licence, and where its source is.
This is the project's reading (docs/design/licences.md in the repository), not legal advice.

1. rkzc itself
   Files: /usr/bin/rkzc-detect, /usr/bin/rkzc-check, /usr/sbin/rkzc-fetch-*, librkzc.so*,
          /usr/include/rkzc/, the Python module rkzc, the service file, the example configuration
   Licence: Apache License 2.0 (on Debian and Ubuntu: /usr/share/common-licenses/Apache-2.0)
   Source: https://github.com/eunkyo3/rk3588s-zero-copy, commit @RKZC_COMMIT@
   Its post-processing code follows Rockchip's rknn_model_zoo v2.3.2 (Apache License 2.0).

2. FFmpeg, as ffmpeg-rockchip
   Files: /opt/rkzc/lib/libavcodec.so.*, libavformat.so.*, libavutil.so.*, libswresample.so.*
   Licence: GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 or later. This build was configured with
          --enable-version3 and without --enable-gpl or --enable-nonfree. The texts are beside this
          file: COPYING.LGPLv3 and COPYING.GPLv3 (the LGPL v3 adds to the GPL v3); on Debian and
          Ubuntu also /usr/share/common-licenses/LGPL-3 and GPL-3.
   Source: https://github.com/nyanmisaka/ffmpeg-rockchip, commit @FFMPEG_COMMIT@.
          The exact source is the archive @FFMPEG_ARCHIVE@,
          published with this package in the same Release of the repository in 1
          (https://github.com/eunkyo3/rk3588s-zero-copy/releases).
   Configured with:
          @FFMPEG_CONFIGURE@
   Changes: none to the source. The installed libraries are the build's, with the run path changed
          from the build's directory to $ORIGIN (lib/packaging/set_runpath.py in the repository in 1)
          and the symbols that linking does not need stripped.
   To use your own build: replace the files in /opt/rkzc/lib with libraries of the same sonames.
          rkzc links them dynamically and finds them there by its run path. So that dpkg does not
          put its own back at the next upgrade, divert each file first:
            dpkg-divert --local --rename --add /opt/rkzc/lib/libavcodec.so.61

3. Not in this package
   - Rockchip's NPU runtime, /opt/rkzc/lib/librknnrt.so: downloaded at install from
     https://github.com/airockchip/rknn-toolkit2 (tag v2.3.2) by rkzc-fetch-runtime. Its licence
     states "All rights reserved" and grants no right to redistribute, so it is fetched from
     Rockchip, not passed on. No header of it is in this package.
   - The models: fetched by rkzc-fetch-model from the repository's Releases, by your choice. They
     derive from Ultralytics YOLOv8 and THU-MIG YOLOv10 and are under the GNU AGPL 3.0.
   - MPP (librockchip-mpp1) and librga (librga2): the image's own packages, which this one depends on.
